kept.what_to_change:
When a document (not an image) is attached, 0.12's `chat_completion_files_handler` runs before the main answer, unless every file is in full-context mode:
1. a blocking `generate_queries` LLM call to the task model (Gemma);
2. a bge-m3 embedding;
3. hybrid search with the bge-reranker-v2-m3 running on CPU.

For one user with a 128k context, prefer full context. Set `RAG_FULL_CONTEXT=True` (Admin > Settings > Documents > Full Context Mode). Alternatively set `BYPASS_EMBEDDING_AND_RETRIEVAL=True` if you never need vector search over files. At minimum, set `ENABLE_RETRIEVAL_QUERY_GENERATION=False`. Keep `RAG_SYSTEM_CONTEXT=False`.

If you still need large knowledge bases, keep retrieval only for those and lower `RAG_TOP_K_RERANKER`.

1) Create a workspace model 'Sarob Auto' (base = the Gemma connection model). Give it Function Calling = Native, the vision capability, and ALL of your tools, skills and filters attached. Leave its system prompt empty. Routed requests take the target model's system prompt and params, so the existing Sarob, Sarob Tez and Sarob Pro models keep their own. 2) Add a Function of type Filter, e.g. 'sarob_router', and attach it only to Sarob Auto, not as a global filter. Set a priority valve so it runs first (lower priority values run first). Skeleton:

class Filter:
  class Valves(BaseModel): priority:int=-10; fast:str='sarob-tez'; think:str='sarob'; pro:str='sarob-pro'
  def __init__(self): self.valves=self.Valves(); self.sticky={}
  async def inlet(self, body, __metadata__=None, __event_emitter__=None):
    tier = self.route(body, (__metadata__ or {}).get('chat_id'))
    body['model'] = {'fast':self.valves.fast,'think':self.valves.think,'pro':self.valves.pro}[tier]
    if __event_emitter__: await __event_emitter__({'type':'status','data':{'description':f'Model: {tier}','done':True}})
    return body

Replace the IDs with your real workspace model IDs from Admin > Models. Do not route with a Pipe. In 0.12, Model controls do not work on pipes. A pipe that runs its own tools must also avoid emitting delta.tool_calls, or Open WebUI's tool loop re-invokes it. Do not use Arena models: they pick at random, and 0.12 turns them off by default on new installs.
